    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T06:34:15Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main f519445d4, except for the open maintainer decision. No code change is necessary for the \"refuse with the measured accuracy\" outcome.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- PR #3259 merged as f2c443540. It preserves a validated short edge when healing makes the endpoint gap exceed the limit.\n- `crates/kernel/tests/step_short_edge.rs` pins the edge count and the endpoint gap before and after healing (`preserve_short_edge_when_healing_would_make_the_gap_exceed_the_limit`, `still_accept_a_healed_box_whose_gap_meets_the_limit`).\n- `refuse_short_edge_model_when_its_source_gap_exceeds_the_limit` pins the outcome when the source exceeds the limit. The refusal gives the source gap, the limit, the edge index, the vertex coordinates and the healed gap. Thus the user can see which check failed and the measured gap.\n- The mesher still checks the requested chord tolerance. Machining checks keep the accuracy that the importer achieved.\n\nWhat stays open: a reduced-fidelity view for a source that exceeds machining tolerance. That is new design work, not a defect fix. It needs the maintainer's decision.\n\nSuggest closing with f2c443540. If the maintainer wants the reduced-fidelity view, file it as a separate `P8` issue. The maintainer decides.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
