    "body": "Issue sweep: partly done on `upstream/main`.\n\nPR #3259 (`f2c443540`, commits `7fd89ffe9` and `a65a65671`) finished the short-edge recovery and the refusal report:\n\n- `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step/record.rs` keeps validated original STEP edges when healing removes edges and creates a gap above 0.001 mm.\n- `crates/kernel/tests/step_short_edge.rs` pins edge counts, endpoint gaps, refusal details, and Level 2 validation (`preserve_short_edge_when_healing_would_make_the_gap_exceed_the_limit`, `still_accept_a_healed_box_whose_gap_meets_the_limit`, `refuse_short_edge_model_when_its_source_gap_exceeds_the_limit`, `refuse_an_unhealed_source_with_an_open_gap_between_curves`).\n\nWhat stays open: the maintainer decision on a reduced-fidelity view when the unhealed source exceeds the 0.001 mm limit. That decision sets whether the current refusal test pins the agreed outcome, or whether CamCraft needs a reduced-fidelity path.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
